Description: pco: shrink vecs whose sources are vectors too
 pco_emit_nir_smp() pads the sampler data to 16 components and passes the
 real size as RANGE; lower_smp() then uses only RANGE channels. The vec of
 a 2D sample starts with the coordinate vec2 and continues with 14 undef
 scalars, so pco_shrink_vecs() skipped it (only_uncollated_elems()), and
 each such sample wrote 14 zero registers. Shrink any vec instead, as long as
 the used channels end on a source boundary.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
